{
	"nodes": [
		{
			"id": "header",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Genetics and Neurodevelopment\n\nDomain hub: genetic architecture and measurement, and the developmental programme that builds the nervous system.\n\n[[Genetics and Neurodevelopment Map|Open the domain map]] - snapshot of 2026-09-25; the map's *In this folder* section is the live view.",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 0,
			"width": 1260,
			"height": 170,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g0",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Genetics",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 2378
		},
		{
			"id": "s0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Genetics and Neurodevelopment - Genetics|Genetics index]]**",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 88,
			"color": "#B8A4FF"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Common and rare variants]]**\n*framework* - 5 sources\n\nTwo regimes of genetic architecture and why the distinction changes study design and interpretation.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 508,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[DNA RNA and gene expression]]**\n*structure* - 6 sources\n\nThe molecules of inheritance and how information flows from DNA to protein, including the machinery that makes the flow regulated rather than mechanical.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 762,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Gene-environment interplay and epigenetics]]**\n*framework* - 7 sources\n\nInteraction, correlation and epigenetic marks: how environmental and genetic influences combine, and what the evidence does and does not show.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 1040,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 242,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Genes, environment and polygenic risk]]**\n*framework* - 13 sources\n\nCommon variants, genome-wide association, polygenic scores, fine-mapping and gene-environment interplay as the actual methods behind inheritance claims.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 1342,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_4",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Genetic inference and polygenic scores]]**\n*method* - 6 sources\n\nHow polygenic scores are built and validated, why transfer across populations is limited, and what individual-level inference they cannot support.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 1620,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 242,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_5",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Genome-wide association studies]]**\n*method* - 3 sources\n\nHow GWAS works, what an association peak means, and the inference steps between a signal and a mechanism.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 1922,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_6",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Inheritance and variation]]**\n*framework* - 7 sources\n\nMendelian patterns, de novo variation, and how family and twin designs estimate genetic contribution.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 2176,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_7",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Polygenic scores and prediction]]**\n*method* - 6 sources\n\nWhat a polygenic score estimates, how it is validated, and the boundary between group-level research use and individual prediction.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 2430,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g1",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Development",
			"x": 420,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 1266
		},
		{
			"id": "s1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Genetics and Neurodevelopment - Development|Development index]]**",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 88,
			"color": "#B8A4FF"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Axon guidance and synaptogenesis]]**\n*process* - 4 sources\n\nHow growing axons find targets using attractive and repulsive cues, and how initial synapses are formed and refined.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 508,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Neurogenesis and migration]]**\n*process* - 4 sources\n\nHow neurons are generated and reach their destinations, and why the framework for adult neurogenesis is more limited than popular accounts suggest.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 762,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Sensitive periods]]**\n*process* - 3 sources\n\nWindows of heightened experience-dependent plasticity, the circuit mechanisms that open and close them, and the limits of the evidence.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 1040,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Synaptic pruning and myelination]]**\n*process* - 6 sources\n\nExperience-dependent elimination of synapses and the progressive myelination of tracts, and why both change functional connectivity.",
			"x": 450,
			"y": 1318,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"color": "#43C6D6"
		},
		{
